codex
Implemented a native Track B bounded two-way partition generator based on the paper’s carry-free integer-block technique.

Key results:

- 12/12 planted witnesses verify.
- Structured guessing: 0/200,000; exact density \(5.66\times10^{-11}\).
- Five adversarial attacks: 0/8 successes each.
- Reference meet-in-the-middle: 8/8, averaging 2,295,171 operations and 4.16 seconds.
- Compact route: at most 187 exact operations.
- Answer: 109 characters, 38 atoms.
- Canonicalization: 60/60 transformations invariant; 20/20 unrelated instances distinct.

Files:

- [gen_2603_12999.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.12999/gen_2603_12999.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.12999/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.12999/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.12999/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.12999/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2603.12999/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Completion is blocked only by OpenRouter: every official harness call returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)`. The transcripts therefore contain script-produced error rows, not scored hardness evidence. `submit.sh` confirms all nine local gates pass but correctly rejects the invalid oracle transcript.

Once the OpenRouter account limit is restored, rerun the bare and two G9 harness arms; no paper rejection is warranted.
